WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.875
Now let's see the safer outer-join pattern The first
ON condition matches

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:10.522
lab rows to patients by patient ID The second ON
condition says

00:00:10.535 --> 00:00:15.632
that only lab rows named Glucose are allowed to
match Run the

00:00:15.658 --> 00:00:20.542
query and count the patient IDs Every patient should
still appear because

00:00:20.569 --> 00:00:26.165
the LEFT JOIN preserves the patient table Then
inspect the lab columns

00:00:27.089 --> 00:00:30.562
Patients who have a glucose result show a test ID
and value

00:00:31.484 --> 00:00:34.457
Patients who do not have a glucose test remain in
the result

00:00:34.747 --> 00:00:39.608
but their lab fields are NULL This is the key idea
the

00:00:39.635 --> 00:00:45.733
filter changes matching not preservation Before you
run the query predict

00:00:45.759 --> 00:00:50.999
which patients will have non-null glucose values
After it runs compare your

00:00:51.012 --> 00:00:55.657
prediction with the output If you use pgAdmin copy
the query and

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:56.893
test it there as well
